From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phononenom <64574232+Phononenom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:44:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the game's memory, packed and
 read through when the console runs short

The guest memory service (src/guest_memory_service.inc, src/memory_pages.cpp): the game's 4 GiB is backed
where it is used in 2 MiB slots; cold slots are packed with LZ4 or zstd (EDEN_CRAM_CODEC, Playtendoh's
Settings > Memory packing) when the pool runs short; a reserve of free blocks serves writes
(EDEN_CRAM_RESERVE_MIB); a write waits for a block instead of failing (EDEN_GUEST_WRITE_WAIT_MS) and counts
how long it waited for the give-back; reads of packed memory go through a window without unpacking when
free memory is low (EDEN_CRAM_READ_THROUGH_MIB, =wide/=wait); sparse commits recover memory before they
give up; contended faults are counted apart. The fastmem handler and its checks follow.

From these commits (oldest first):
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: guest memory is packed on demand, not by the scanner's passes
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the memory reports count the title's page tables
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: untouched guest memory takes no page tables until it is read
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: short-lived views stay out of the heap's address range
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a sparse slot the pool has no room for is asked for again
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a table slot the pool refuses comes from the guest memory reserve
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap gives memory back without a gap
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a slot that does not compress is not packed again until written
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a JIT code step the pool refuses takes the guest memory reserve
- 2026-11-18 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a writer waiting for a block wakes the scanner to pack
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the compaction is asked where memory runs short
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the give-back is asked for while the reserve stays short
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the graphics threads keep their blocks for the give-back
- 2026-11-21 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: game memory packed with LZ4 or zstd, chosen per session
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the read-through window only while a game write waits
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the read-through window opens when the pool is near its end
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: a write fault that finds its slot being changed is no repeat
